  "reason": "Evidence: RNA (PCA n2000, single profile) achieves 0.485 accuracy while Image (ResNet50, single profile) only reaches 0.208, indicating RNA is the dominant modality and the primary path to improvement. Uncertainty: We don't yet know whether a learned RNA encoder (scvi_n200) can outperform the simple PCA baseline, or whether the 0.485 is near the ceiling for this modality. This experiment (config_004: RNA-only, single profile, scvi_n200) directly compares against config_001 by changing only the RNA encoder, isolating the effect of representation learning. If scvi_n200 improves accuracy, it justifies further investment in learned encoders and multiprofile variants; if it does not, PCA is sufficient and we should pivot to testing multiprofile aggregation or multimodal fusion. With 7 experiments remaining, this clean single-variable test is the most informative next step before committing budget to more complex multimodal or multiprofile configurations."
